Z||000000||N_Man||05-15-2000||11:15 AM||||Starting to drop the cradle today but I already have one question.<BR>Since the cradle is coming out I cant jack the car anywhere on the cradle, so im wondering where is the best place to jack the rear of the car from?<BR>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spyder||05-15-2000||11:23 AM||||I jack the rear up on the rear cradle and then put jack stands on a rail looking ledges near where the front engine cradle mounts are. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-15-2000||10:49 PM||||I did the same as Spyder.  I placed the battery in the spare tire well to help balance the car when I dropped the cradle.  With the jack stands on the front cradle support points the car tends to want to see-saw on you if you forget and lean on the rear a bit too much.||||reg||1
